# Ports scripts/agent-sandbox.zsh publishes for this project's container — one
# container port per line, 1-65535; `#` starts a comment. Each becomes
# `-p 127.0.0.1::<port>`: reachable from the host only (loopback), on an
# EPHEMERAL host port so several containers never collide. `agent-sandbox-ports`
# (or `docker port <container> <port>`) shows the mapping. Changes apply at
# the next agent-sandbox-recreate / agent-sandbox-rebuild. One invalid line rejects the file.
#
# This file is read on the HOST and sits under the read-only .devcontainer
# overlay, so the agent can't publish ports for itself. Per-project:
# sync-harness.sh copies it only when missing. Ignored by the VS Code path,
# which auto-forwards ports instead.
#
